# Jak 1's Load Game (LIST-0.1.3 item 1; players: "load still seems like it starts new game in jak 1"). Start opens the
# title menu with the right hand pointing into it and shaking a little (0.3 degrees every 4 frames, a hand held still
# on a headset). B first: on the title it is back (Triangle since 0.1.3), the game's own: the menu closes to PRESS
# START and nothing is chosen (to 0.1.2 it was Circle, which Jak 1's menus take as Cross: New Game; sim b54 load1);
# Start opens it again (l-reopened). Then the left stick down once to Load Game and A: the save files
# (l-files; the save tests/jak1_make_save.sim made in the first file: the batch runs that first, both with their own
# config folder and KEEP_SAVES=1, since the runner otherwise clears the saves); B there goes back to the title with
# Load Game still lit (l-back; sim b55: a second stick-down went on to Options), A again, A on the first file: it
# loads (l-loaded, Jak where the save left him, not the new game's opening). Run with JAKVR_POINTER_TRACE=1
# JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1.
